  - photon blockade
  - QuTiP
abstract: >-
  QuTiP and NumPy simulations of the Jaynes-Cummings model, with the
  manuscripts they support. (1) Wigner-function dynamics and cat-state
  formation at half the revival time, atom-field entanglement (reduced
  entropy and logarithmic negativity) for coherent, thermal, squeezed and
  Fock initial fields, decoherence under cavity loss, a cat-state survival
  phase diagram, and photon-blockade statistics. (2) "Rotation and shear in
  the Jaynes-Cummings model": the second order of the expansion of the Rabi
  frequencies shears each field component by an amount equal to its rotation
  angle; closed forms for the revival heights, the parity at half the revival
  time, the cat fidelity, the squeezing, the Wigner negativity and the
  residual entanglement are tested against the exact solution, together with
  measured errors of the numerical methods and an exploratory extension to
  finite detuning. Every figure, table and animation is generated by the
  scripts in simulations/.
